<title>SYRIA: Syria offers 40,000 tonnes of wheat for sale.</title>
<headline>Syria offers 40,000 tonnes of wheat for sale.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's General Establishment for Cereal Processing and Trade (GECPT) has offered 40,000 tonnes of hard durum amber wheat for sale, a company spokesman said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>He said an international call setting February 12 as the final date for bids had already been issued. Confirmation would be made on February 13.</p>
<p>The grain, from the 1995 crop, would be ready for shipment in March.</p>
<p>Partial offers would be accepted.</p>
</text>
